Description: Return NULL from TrackerResource print functions on invalid input.
 tracker_resource_print_turtle(), tracker_resource_print_sparql_update() and
 tracker_resource_print_jsonld() returned a string literal when given something which is not a
 TrackerResource, although the caller owns the result and frees it. Freeing it aborted with
 "free(): invalid pointer", which crashed the localsearch extractor. They return NULL instead,
 like tracker_resource_print_rdf() does, and a test covers all three.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/tinysparql/-/merge_requests/819
Last-Update: 2026-11-01
